	"claims": [
		{
			"id": "R9-software-projection",
			"statement": "Independently inspect and execute the current repaired block projection. Check Euclidean and width-weighted metrics, exact zero-normal handling, extreme scaling and invalid finite/dimension/width inputs. Reproduce the actual historical AST projection failure on unequal widths, the supplied exact SL counterexample, and the real n2R4 source-case first variation. Verify tangency is checked with separate direct integration, not merely the constructed dot product.",
			"verification": "software"
		},
		{
			"id": "R9-software-integration",
			"statement": "Independently execute meaningful checks of true block endpoint integration, weighted normalization, unweighted spectral pairings and the second-variation sum. Re-run normal/-O regressions and the four required CLI cases, checking candidate/dependency hashes against supplied snapshots. Test the no-clamping finite-difference positivity guard, retained CLI defaults and R=1 behavior. Runtime missing evidence is INCOMPLETE, not approval. Work in a fresh private copied input tree, never author/current live source outside the packet.",
			"verification": "software"
		},
		{
			"id": "R9-software-scope",
			"statement": "Check actual cutoff, quadrature and FD sensitivity and honest remaining numerical errors, including the small INF direction and double-precision cancellation. Inspect P2b changes separately from the block-average bug. Check P3 fixed-width direction breakpoints and half-interface acceleration sign/factor, without inferring an eta limit or universal Hessian identity. Verify report counts/residuals/signs match actual data, tests reject bad controls under -O, and no sampled sign is called a proof of definiteness or box-constrained optimality.",
			"verification": "numerical"
		}
	],
